  "background_and_question": {
    "claims": [
      {
        "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "88cbd20d6f734af8779f4db2f4b5ae3a560d8e8a203b40d695cd8af78dfff22d",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-88cbd20d6f73-0000-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 4,
              "start": 4
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Chief Justice Roberts asked whether there should be limits on the type of loyalty oath the government can require organizations to sign."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "88cbd20d6f734af8779f4db2f4b5ae3a560d8e8a203b40d695cd8af78dfff22d",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-88cbd20d6f73-0001-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 27,
              "start": 27
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Kennedy asked what case would give the Court extra deference because the issue involves foreign affairs."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "88cbd20d6f734af8779f4db2f4b5ae3a560d8e8a203b40d695cd8af78dfff22d",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-88cbd20d6f73-0001-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 29,
              "start": 29
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Chief Justice Roberts, chief Justice Roberts questioned whether the government is merely selecting partners who share its opposition to prostitution."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "88cbd20d6f734af8779f4db2f4b5ae3a560d8e8a203b40d695cd8af78dfff22d",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-88cbd20d6f73-0001-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 32,
              "start": 32
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Kennedy, justice Kennedy raised a question about whether Congress can prefer one organization over another because it likes the organization\u2019s policies."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "88cbd20d6f734af8779f4db2f4b5ae3a560d8e8a203b40d695cd8af78dfff22d",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-88cbd20d6f73-0001-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 38,
              "start": 38
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Sotomayor asked where the line is drawn between the government\u2019s funding conditions and promoting the legalization of prostitution."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice SOTOMAYOR",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "88cbd20d6f734af8779f4db2f4b5ae3a560d8e8a203b40d695cd8af78dfff22d",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-88cbd20d6f73-0002-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 40,
              "start": 40
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Sotomayor further asked whether it would be permissible for an organization to distribute literature that promotes the legalization of prostitution."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice KENNEDY",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "88cbd20d6f734af8779f4db2f4b5ae3a560d8e8a203b40d695cd8af78dfff22d",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-88cbd20d6f73-0002-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 46,
              "start": 46
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice KENNEDY, justice Kennedy posed a hypothetical about a malaria program and whether Congress may choose a quieter organization over a more effective but critical one."
      }
    ],
